  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let \\(ABC\\) be a right-angled triangle with \\(\\angle ABC=90^\\circ\\). Let \\(P\\) be the midpoint of \\(BC\\) and \\(Q\\) be a point on \\(AB\\). Suppose that the length of \\(BC\\) is \\(2x\\), \\(\\angle ACQ=\\alpha\\), and \\(\\angle APQ=\\beta\\). Then the length of \\(AQ\\) is",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac{3x}{2\\cot\\alpha-\\cot\\beta}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac{2x}{3\\cot\\alpha-2\\cot\\beta}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac{3x}{\\cot\\alpha-2\\cot\\beta}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{2x}{2\\cot\\alpha-3\\cot\\beta}\\)"
  },
  "answer": "A",
